  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health system strengthening programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;b&gt;Healthcare&lt;/b&gt; stands for Health system strengthening programme and its main objective is to support Rwanda in its transformation to a well governed, climate resilient and inclusive welfare state. It supports the implementation of the national health sector policy and health strategy, and the current and future sub-sector strategies, in particular on MNCH (Maternal, Newborn and Child Health), Family Planning-ASRH (Adolescent Sexual and Reproductive Health), NCD (Non-Communicable Diseases) including Mental Health and Nutrition. The alignment to national strategies will strengthen the sustainability of this support.</narrative>
  </description>
